<title>UK: LME de-lists zinc and tin brands.</title>
<headline>LME de-lists zinc and tin brands.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>The London Metal Exchange (LME) is to de-list brands of Japanese zinc and Indonesian tin when respective stocks have been run down.</p>
<p>At its regular Board meeting the LME decided that from March 11 1997 no further deliveries of Japan's MSC special high grade zinc and Indonesian KOBA tin will be accepted for warranting.</p>
<p>Once the stocks warranted as of March 10 1997 are exhausted the brands will be de-listed, it said.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom, +44 171 542 8080</p>
</text>
